{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-26T14:26:53.749Z","data":{"text":"I've completed task 4. Here's a summary:\n\n## What I did\n\n**Core implementation:**\n- `src/core/spec/approve.ts` — `approveSpec` now lints then dispatches: with `vcs.enabled` + `GitVcs` it calls `approveIntoWorktree`, otherwise the in-place path. Extracted `approveInPlace`, added `worktreePath`/`branch` to `ApproveResult`, added `baseOk`/`ignoreDirty` to `ApproveOptions`, and moved seal writes to a shared helper.\n- `src/core/spec/approve-worktree.ts` (new) — four refusals (non-default HEAD, dirty task scope, existing branch, unlanded approved dependency) run after lint and before the digest; then branch/worktree creation, `vcs.prepare` in the worktree, recursive copy of the change folder, observation append, `.run/approved` + `.run/base` + `.run/approver` + manifest, and the commit via a second `selectVcs`.\n- `src/core/spec/approve-worktree-shared.ts` (new) — shared seal/review gate and approval types (kept acyclic).\n\n**CLI/docs:**\n- `src/cli/approve.ts` — `registerApproveCommand` with `--confirm`, `--base-ok`, `--ignore-dirty`; prints `  Worktree:` and `  Branch:` lines.\n- `src/cli/index.ts` — delegates to `registerApproveCommand`.\n- `README.md` — documents both new flags.\n\n**Tests:** `tests/approve-worktree.test.ts` covers all 7 delta scenarios plus vcs-off approval and CLI flag registration.\n\n## Verification\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/approve-worktree.test.ts` → 9/9 pass\n- `pnpm verify` → full typecheck, UI typecheck, build, entire suite, and lint pass\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/089-approve-into-worktree/.run/results/4.md`."}}
